{
  "openapi": "3.1.0",
  "info": {
    "title": "Opteryx Jobs Service",
    "version": "0.1.0"
  },
  "x-flow": {
    "title": "Job flow",
    "intro": "Jobs run asynchronously: submitting a query returns immediately with an `execution_id`, and the query keeps running in the background until you poll it to completion.",
    "actors": [
      "Client",
      "Jobs API"
    ],
    "steps": [
      {
        "request": "POST /api/v1/jobs"
      },
      {
        "response": "201",
        "returns": "`execution_id`, `status`, `status_url`"
      },
      {
        "group": "Loop — poll until finished",
        "steps": [
          {
            "request": "GET /api/v1/jobs/{execution_id}/status"
          },
          {
            "response": "200",
            "returns": "`status`, `results_url`"
          }
        ],
        "note": "Repeat on an interval until `status` is no longer in progress"
      },
      {
        "request": "GET /api/v1/jobs/{execution_id}/results"
      },
      {
        "response": "200",
        "returns": "`data[]`, `total_rows`, `next_page`"
      },
      {
        "group": "Or, to export instead",
        "steps": [
          {
            "request": "GET /api/v1/jobs/{execution_id}/download?file_format=csv|json|parquet"
          },
          {
            "response": "200",
            "returns": "file"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "notes": [
      "**Poll `status`, not `results`.** `GET .../status` is cheap and returns `results_url` once the job is done; `GET .../results` is what actually pages through the data, `num_rows`/`offset` at a time, following `next_page` for more.",
      "**`results` and `download` are independent, not exclusive.** Pull a page inline with `results` to inspect it in your app, or stream the whole set with `download` as CSV, newline-delimited JSON, or Parquet — call either, neither, or both once the job has finished."
    ]
  },
